{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788491730,"nonce":"GM21WI8N+d+n3QIWqag+K0ei0Xw=","title":"Who did it, and what was destroyed: provenance on every journal row, and a destroy event","message":"Part of the cockpit round, b4adee2. Design: RUNS/openrun-20260902/audit/COCKPIT.md\n§When the clock stops and §Where it lives (in the mod). The screen spec depends\non this one, which is why it is first in the order.\n\nWHAT\n\nTwo additions to the journal.\n\n1. A `destroyed` event for player-faction buildings and frames, and for\n   corpses, carrying def, id, position and the game's own DestroyMode. Hooks:\n   Building.Destroy (Verse/Building.cs), Frame.Destroy (RimWorld/Frame.cs),\n   Corpse.Destroy. Thing.Destroy is NOT patched — it is hot on every stack merge\n   (a8d8ada's caution stands). A destroyed player building stops a running\n   advance the way a casualty does; a corpse does not.\n\n   The audit's fact behind it: the journal has fifteen event types and none is\n   \"something was destroyed\". When a manhunter pack destroyed two turrets and\n   an autocannon, the journal recorded nothing; the agent rebuilt the two it\n   counted and never learned the third was gone. Its own account names that as\n   the first link in the chain that ended the colony (themes.md T3, findings\n   F-S12-13/14).\n\n2. A `by` field on every journal row: `agent` (emitted inside the poller's\n   drain, with the command id), `mod` (inside a chore), `game` (inside the tick),\n   `human` (a mutation reached from the game's own input handlers while nothing\n   of ours is running). Human actions themselves become `action` rows with\n   by:human and the game's own label for what was pressed.\n\n   The audit's fact behind it: Dorian intervened at least 22 times — a revival\n   through the debug menu, a deleted weather event, 411 meals, nine in-game days\n   played by hand — and nothing marks any of it (themes.md T13, T14). Three of\n   the run's 23 death rows are debug-menu residue and one death was reversed\n   with no row for the reversal, so no count from this run is a measurement.\n\nSCOPE\n\n- Provenance is one static value set at three sites — the drain, the chores,\n  the tick — and read by every existing hook. Default outside all three is\n  human.\n- Human actions: postfixes on DesignatorManager.ProcessInputEvents\n  (Verse/DesignatorManager.cs), Command.ProcessInput (Verse/Command.cs),\n  FloatMenuOption.Chosen (Verse/FloatMenuOption.cs), DebugActionNode.Enter\n  (LudeonTK/DebugActionNode.cs), and the dialog button paths. Verify each\n  member by name in the decompiled source before building; line numbers differ\n  between the two boxes.\n- A revival through the debug menu is a row; today John's first death stands\n  unqualified in the journal while he died again 5.5 million ticks later.\n- dev:* verbs keep their `dev` rows and are by:agent.\n- The screen folds a long human stretch to \"N actions over M ticks\", with the\n  rows behind `journal`. How nine hand-played days should read is UNKNOWN and\n  this is the proposal.\n\nACCEPTANCE\n\n- dev:destroy a wall, a turret and a corpse during an advance on a bench: three\n  `destroyed` rows carrying the DestroyMode the game passed; the advance halts\n  on the building rows and not on the corpse row.\n- On the bench with the window shown: place a designation with the mouse, spawn\n  a thing from the debug menu, and revive a dead pawn from it. Three rows with\n  by:human, and the next screen's human row lists all three.\n- A death caused by a chore, by the game, and by an agent verb carry by:mod,\n  by:game and by:agent.\n- The audit's zero-prior-row test (themes.md T13) is re-run on the next run's\n  journal and finds no death without provenance.\n- The Building.Destroy postfix is timed on the 38-mod bench across a 60,000-tick\n  advance with a fire burning, and the cost is stated in the closing comment.\n\nABSORBS\n\na8d8ada (the corpse half is bullet 1 exactly, DestroyMode reported and never\nturned into a story); the building-destroyed half of f1a1700 (its room-role\nhalf stays a stated limit in the screen spec). The provenance half of T13/T14\nwas unfiled before this issue.","files":null}]}